[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Version=1.0
Name=TerraByte 최초 설정 마법사
Name[en]=TerraByte First-Boot Setup Wizard
Comment=아두이노·와이파이·신원을 확인하고 등록 번호를 안내합니다
# XDG autostart has no conditional field, so the "first boot only" decision is
# made by the shell guard below instead of by enabling/disabling this file.
# Deleting the entry after setup would work too, but then a re-run would need
# someone to remember where the file came from; the marker file is the single
# source of truth and `rm` on it is the documented way to start over.
#
# The env file is sourced with `set -a` because /etc/terrabyte-edge.env stores
# bare KEY=value lines (systemd EnvironmentFile syntax) that would otherwise stay
# shell-local and never reach python. Sourcing usually FAILS here and that is
# fine: the file is root-owned 0640 because it holds the MQTT password, so the
# desktop user cannot read it. The wizard then takes its identity from the
# status snapshot the bridge publishes (0644), which carries the same gateway id
# and claim code loaded from that very env file.
Exec=sh -c "[ -e /var/lib/terrabyte-edge/setup-complete ] && exit 0; set -a; [ -r /etc/terrabyte-edge.env ] && . /etc/terrabyte-edge.env; set +a; exec /opt/terrabyte-edge/.venv/bin/python -m terrabyte_edge wizard"
Terminal=false
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true
# Starts ahead of the dashboard (delay 5) on purpose. Both are full-screen Tk
# windows and whichever maps last takes focus; the wizard must be the one the
# user sees at a first boot, and by the time it exits the dashboard is up.
X-GNOME-Autostart-Delay=2
